        "original_id": "030ea317-75d6-55ed-a5f0-3714602dba9f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Frank Pepe Pizzeria Napoletana, Sarpino's Pizzeria, Foxon Park\n- Places: Wooster Square, New Haven, Connecticut, Singapore, Lincolnshire, Illinois\n- Products: New Haven-style pizza, soda\n- Restaurants: Sally's Apizza, Modern Apizza, Louis' Lunch\n- Topics: pizza restaurants, fast food chains\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Pepe Pizzeria Napoletana is a popular pizza restaurant located at 163 Wooster Street in the Wooster Square neighborhood of New Haven, Connecticut.\n- Frank Pepe Pizzeria Napoletana is known locally as Pepe's.\n- New Haven-style pizza originated at Frank Pepe Pizzeria Napoletana.\n- New Haven-style pizza is now served at many pizza restaurants in the New Haven area, including Sally's Apizza and Modern Apizza.\n- Sarpino's Pizzeria is a fast food restaurant chain that specializes in pizza.\n- Sarpino's Pizzeria has its international operations headquartered in Singapore.\n- Sarpino's Pizzeria has its U.S. operations headquartered in Lincolnshire, Illinois.\n- Foxon Park sodas are a traditional accompaniment to New Haven-style pizza sold throughout the area.\n- Foxon Park sodas are also served at Louis' Lunch.",
